# held/weapons/bow_crossbow: the crossbow (art weapon 3 with bow form 4, `held bow.crossbow`): a 12 x 10 bow, the ash tiller (2 px of wood) and a steel prod across its nose (the prod draws in the blade metal), a linen string, a brass nut; the bolt steel with a white point (P2c wave 2, WEAPONS). STYLE_P2 11 / 25.7; P2C_CONTRACTS 4: the library weapon on the grip,
# a000..a337 = degrees counter-clockwise from screen-right, drawn once (D) for every facing; on the bow hand (gripL: the left fist on the fore-stock); origin = the grip point
# under the main fist (the hand is drawn over the grip); `mark tip` at the far end. Drafted with the area's stepper (exact
# 1:0, 2:1, 1:1 and 1:2 runs, the top-left light by rule: a 2 px band's upper / left line lit) and hand-cleaned at 12x.
# Finish regions (contracts 3b): R the nut, N the bolt.
use person
legend V linen 0
legend W linen 1
legend X linen 2
legend Y linen 3
legend Z linen 4
body adult
role held bow.crossbow
layer held
anchor gripL
keys held
tags anyfacing
